# spelling -> canonical: how found (after the hand reading)
"IP" -> trunc: same body: _INT: floor for a proven x >= 0, ceil for a proven x < 0, each part of a complex (trunc's split; an exact integer)
"FP" -> fPart: same body: FP: g-_INT(g), fPart's body (fPart also maps a list)
"ABS" -> abs: same body: _ABS: abs, a list's l2norm (norm)
"SIGN" -> sign: same body: sign, the function _sign maps over a list

